&lt;div class=&quot;mb-8&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;text-2xl font-medium mb-4 text-white&quot;&gt;About Noble Machines&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;text-gray-300&quot;&gt;Noble Machines (formerly Under Control Robotics) builds multipurpose robots to support human workers in the world&#39;s toughest jobs—turning dangerous work from a necessity into a choice. Our work demands reliability, robustness, and readiness for the unexpected—on time, every time. We&#39;re assembling a mission-driven team focused on delivering real impact in heavy industry, from construction and mining to energy. If you&#39;re driven to build rugged, reliable products that solve real-world problems, we&#39;d love to talk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mb-8&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;text-2xl font-medium mb-4 text-white&quot;&gt;Position Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;text-gray-300&quot;&gt;At Noble Machines, building robots is a team sport. As a Robotics Autonomy Engineer, you&#39;ll take ownership and lead the development of autonomy systems that power our multipurpose robots across diverse and unstructured environments. You&#39;ll design, implement, and optimize cutting-edge localization, mapping, navigation, and SLAM systems—including advanced techniques such as 3D Gaussian Splatting, NeRFs, and other neural or volumetric methods—that enable our robots to perceive, understand, and act in the real world with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mb-8&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;text-2xl font-medium mb-4 text-white&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-300&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain real-time mapping, localization, and navigation software for mobility robotic systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable SLAM pipelines using a mix of sensors, including LiDAR, vision, and IMU&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement 3D scene representations using cutting-edge techniques such as 3D Gaussian Splatting, NeRFs, and other neural or volumetric methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate localization and mapping modules with motion planning and control systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy robust autonomy stacks to on-board compute platforms and validate them in both simulation and real-world testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and tune performance of perception and SLAM systems in challenging environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with mechanical, electrical, and software engineers to develop co-designed autonomy solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, modular, production-quality code with thorough documentation and testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate and support robots during field testing and customer deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mb-8&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;text-2xl font-medium mb-4 text-white&quot;&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-300&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience working in robotics, autonomy, or a closely related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundation in SLAM, probabilistic localization, 3D reconstruction, and navigation algorithms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with C++ and Python, especially in real-time robotics or embedded systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and deploying autonomy stacks using frameworks such as ROS or ROS2&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to develop algorithms for sensor fusion and state estimation (e.g., EKF, UKF, particle filters)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with real robot systems—ground, legged, or aerial platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with 3D mapping techniques including voxel grids, mesh reconstruction, and Gaussian Splatting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated rapid growth and technical ownership on complex autonomy projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize and execute tasks in a fast-paced, dynamic environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration skills across disciplines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mb-8&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;text-2xl font-medium mb-4 text-white&quot;&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-300&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GPU-accelerated vision or perception pipelines (CUDA, TensorRT)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to deep learning-based SLAM, view synthesis, or scene understanding techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multirobot SLAM, loop closure, or graph optimization frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to open-source robotics or perception libraries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort debugging hardware/software integration in field settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with autonomy in unstructured or GPS-denied environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of simulation frameworks (e.g., Gazebo, Isaac Sim, Unity Robotics)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;mt-8&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-4 text-gray-300&quot;&gt;To apply, submit your resume here or email people@noblemachines.ai .&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;font-medium&quot;&gt;To increase your chances of being selected for an interview, we encourage you to include a public portfolio of your most representative work featuring your individual contributions and public demonstrations of autonomy or SLAM systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Director of Finance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Sunnyvale, CA (on-site) &lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&lt;/strong&gt; CEO&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Noble Machines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Noble Machines builds multipurpose robots to support human workers in the world&#39;s toughest jobs—turning dangerous work from a necessity into a choice. Our work demands reliability, robustness, and readiness for the unexpected—on time, every time. We&#39;re assembling a mission-driven team focused on delivering real impact in heavy industry, from construction and mining to energy. If you&#39;re driven to build rugged, reliable products that solve real-world problems, we&#39;d love to talk.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring our first Director of Finance to build the financial backbone of the company as we scale. You&#39;ll own financial planning, reporting, and operations end-to-end — partnering directly with the CEO and leadership team to bring clarity and discipline to how we forecast, budget, and make decisions. This is a hands-on, builder role: you&#39;ll be standing up systems and processes from a lean starting point, not inheriting a mature finance org.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own financial planning &amp;amp; analysis: annual and rolling forecasts, long-range planning, scenario modeling, and cash runway management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain budgeting processes and monthly financial reviews with business/functional partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare financial reporting, board materials, and investor updates; support fundraising diligence, data rooms, and investor Q&amp;amp;A&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure accurate financial records in accordance with GAAP; own accounting policies, procedures, and internal controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage cash flow and treasury operations, banking relationships, and monitor compliance with applicable laws, tax filings, and regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate, implement, and own finance systems (e.g., QuickBooks/NetSuite, cap table management, payroll/PEO) as the company scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and mitigate financial and operational risk; develop financial strategies around capital, facilities, and staffing needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering and operations on manufacturing-related finance: BOM costing, unit economics, inventory accounting, capital equipment planning, and supply chain/vendor spend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with People Ops on compensation planning and equity administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a primary point of contact for investors, banking partners, and outside accounting/tax/audit firms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support corporate development activities including strategic partnerships and potential M&amp;amp;A&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7–10+ years of progressive finance experience, including experience at the Controller, Head of Finance, or Director level in a high-growth or startup environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of GAAP, financial reporting, tax, and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling financial operations and internal controls from the ground up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record supporting fundraising, investor relations, and board reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating as a hands-on individual contributor as well as a strategic leader we’re a lean team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Required&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt; background in hardware, manufacturing, or deep tech — including experience with BOM/product costing, inventory accounting, capital equipment budgeting, or supply chain finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with QuickBooks or NetSuite, cap table tools, and Excel/Google Sheets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Finance, Accounting, Business Administration, or related field; MBA, CPA, or Master&#39;s in Finance a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be authorized to work in the U.S.; note this role may require access to information subject to U.S. export control regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Sets a Great Candidate Apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior public accounting experience, spanning both large firms and startups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active CPA license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with equipment financing or other non-dilutive financing structures common to hardware companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a manufacturing environment — e.g., managing costing/margin analysis for physical products, working with contract manufacturers, or overseeing capex for production lines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable pushing a fast but sustainable pace in a fast-paced, resource-constrained environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;California Pay Transparency Statement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pay Transparency &amp;amp; Compensation: In accordance with California&#39;s Pay Transparency Act (SB 1162), the expected base salary range for this position located in Sunnyvale, CA is &lt;strong&gt;$200,000 – $250,000 per year&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Actual compensation within this range will be determined based on several factors, including the candidate&#39;s qualifications, relevant experience, technical skills, and specialized expertise. Base salary is just one component of Noble Machines&#39; total rewards package, which may also include equity options, comprehensive healthcare benefits, retirement plan contributions, and performance-based incentives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Noble Machines is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All employment decisions are based on business needs, job requirements, and individual qualifications, without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, disability status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Electrical Engineer (Embedded Systems &amp;amp; Tools)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Noble Machines · Sunnyvale, CA (On-site)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Noble Machines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Noble Machines builds multipurpose robots to support human workers in the world&#39;s toughest jobs—turning dangerous work from a necessity into a choice. Our work demands reliability, robustness, and readiness for the unexpected—on time, every time. We&#39;re assembling a mission-driven team focused on delivering real impact in heavy industry, from construction and mining to energy. If you&#39;re driven to build rugged, reliable products that solve real-world problems, we&#39;d love to talk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an exceptional Senior Electrical Engineer to design and own the embedded devices and internal tools that power the next generation of Noble Machines&#39; general-purpose robots. This is a high-impact, high-ownership role: you&#39;ll be the person other engineers rely on for reliable hardware and the tooling that makes their own work faster and safer. You&#39;ll work across the full stack — from schematic design and layout to bring-up to field validation — building electronics that have to work the first time, every time, in environments where failure isn&#39;t an option.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own electrical design end-to-end for embedded devices and internal developer tools — schematics, PCB layout, bring-up, and validation — supporting the robot&#39;s compute, sensing, and communication subsystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build test fixtures, debug tooling, and diagnostic hardware that accelerate development and validation across the broader engineering team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect embedded electronics for reliability in harsh field conditions (dust, vibration, temperature extremes, power transients common to construction, mining, and energy sites).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select and integrate microcontrollers, sensors, and communication interfaces (I2C, SPI, CAN, Ethernet, USB) to support real-time control and data acquisition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with mechanical, firmware, and software teams to ensure electrical designs integrate cleanly with the full robot system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own component lifecycle management and vendor relationships, including PCBA fabrication and assembly partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute validation and test plans (DVT/PVT), using lab equipment (oscilloscopes, logic analyzers, power supplies) to verify performance, safety, and reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other engineers on hardware design, documentation, and debugging best practices as the team grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of professional experience in electrical engineering, ideally in robotics, embedded systems, automotive, or consumer/industrial electronics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on PCB design experience (multi-layer, mixed-signal), using tools such as Altium or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with embedded systems: microcontroller-based design, firmware/hardware interfaces, and common communication protocols (I2C, SPI, CAN, UART, Ethernet, USB).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of taking hardware from concept through prototyping, validation, and production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building test fixtures, debug tools, or developer-facing hardware/tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with root-cause debugging of hardware and firmware issues using lab equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills — you&#39;ll be documenting designs and mentoring others, not just building in isolation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s, Master&#39;s, or PhD in Electrical Engineering or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with power electronics: DC/DC converters, motor drives, battery management systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in legged or humanoid robotics, or other complex electromechanical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ROS 2 or embedded Linux/RTOS environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing for ruggedized or explosion-proof/hazardous-area electronics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sensor integration experience (IMUs, encoders, force/torque sensors, LIDAR).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;California Pay Transparency Statement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pay Transparency &amp;amp; Compensation: In accordance with California&#39;s Pay Transparency Act (SB 1162), the expected base salary range for this position located in Sunnyvale, CA is &lt;strong&gt;$185,000 – $215,000 per year&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Actual compensation within this range will be determined based on several factors, including the candidate&#39;s qualifications, relevant experience, technical skills, and specialized expertise. Base salary is just one component of Noble Machines&#39; total rewards package, which may also include equity options, comprehensive healthcare benefits, retirement plan contributions, and performance-based incentives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Noble Machines is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All employment decisions are based on business needs, job requirements, and individual qualifications, without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, disability status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Noble Machines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Noble Machines builds multipurpose robots to support human workers in the world&#39;s toughest jobs—turning dangerous work from a necessity into a choice. Our work demands reliability, robustness, and readiness for the unexpected—on time, every time. We&#39;re assembling a mission-driven team focused on delivering real impact in heavy industry, from construction and mining to energy. If you&#39;re driven to build rugged, reliable products that solve real-world problems, we&#39;d love to talk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Noble Machines is looking for a Forward Deployed Engineer to be the critical link between our robotics platform and the customers putting it to work in the field—construction sites, mines, and energy facilities where the work is hardest and the stakes are highest. You&#39;ll deploy, integrate, and support our robots on-site, troubleshoot issues that span software, hardware, and networking in real time, and feed what you learn in the field directly back into product and engineering. This is a hands-on, high-ownership role for someone who is just as comfortable configuring a system as they are climbing onto equipment or debugging from a jobsite trailer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Lead on-site deployment, installation, and integration of Noble Machines&#39; robots at customer sites across construction, mining, and energy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Serve as the primary technical point of contact for customers during deployment, resolving hardware, software, autonomy, and networking issues in real time under field conditions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Partner with engineering, autonomy, and hardware teams to translate field learnings, edge cases, and customer feedback into concrete product requirements and improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Design and refine scalable deployment processes, tooling, and documentation as Noble Machines&#39; customer base grows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Own technical outcomes end-to-end—from pre-deployment planning and site readiness through go-live, training, and ongoing support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Provide hands-on training to customer operators and site personnel on safe, effective robot operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Conduct root-cause analysis on field incidents and drive fixes across hardware, firmware, and software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Travel regularly to customer sites, including remote and industrial environments, to support deployments and maintain uptime&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Robotics, or a related technical field, or equivalent hands-on experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; 3+ years of experience solving problems at the intersection of hardware, software, and networking, ideally in unstructured or field environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Proficiency in Python and/or C++, with the ability to read, debug, and modify code across the stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Comfort working hands-on with physical systems—wiring, sensors, mechanical troubleshooting—in addition to software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Strong ownership mentality and the ability to work independently on ambiguous, high-stakes problems with shifting requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Excellent communication skills, with the ability to build trust with customers in high-pressure field environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Willingness to travel frequently to industrial and remote job sites, including construction sites, mines, and energy facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Ability to perform physical tasks associated with fieldwork (e.g., lifting equipment, working outdoors in varied conditions, wearing required PPE)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Experience deploying robotics, autonomy, or hardware products in heavy industry (construction, mining, oil &amp;amp; gas, utilities)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Familiarity with ROS/ROS2, autonomy stacks, or robot fleet management systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Linux systems administration, networking, and on-prem/edge deployment experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Background in defense, automotive, or industrial robotics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Relevant safety certifications (OSHA 10/30, MSHA, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;California Pay Transparency Statement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pay Transparency &amp;amp; Compensation: In accordance with California&#39;s Pay Transparency Act (SB 1162), the expected base salary range for this position located in Sunnyvale, CA is $140,000 – $195,000 per year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Actual compensation within this range will be determined based on several factors, including the candidate&#39;s qualifications, relevant experience, technical skills, and specialized expertise. Base salary is just one component of Noble Machines&#39; total rewards package, which may also include equity options, comprehensive healthcare benefits, retirement plan contributions, and performance-based incentives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Noble Machines is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All employment decisions are based on business needs, job requirements, and individual qualifications, without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, disability status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;About Noble Machines&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Noble Machines (formerly Under Control Robotics, UCR) builds general-purpose robots that take on hazardous and physically demanding industrial tasks, enabling a safer, more efficient, and more productive world. Our work demands reliability, robustness, and readiness for the unexpected—on time, every time. We&#39;re assembling a mission-driven team focused on delivering real impact in heavy industry, from construction and mining to manufacturing and energy. If you&#39;re driven to build rugged, reliable products that solve real-world problems, we&#39;d love to talk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Position Overview&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Noble Machines, building robots is a team sport. As a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Test Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;, you will own the validation of our multipurpose humanoid robots across &lt;strong&gt;hardware, software, and AI systems&lt;/strong&gt;. You will operate the robot directly to stress test real-world performance, design and execute test plans, analyze logs and data, and produce clear reports that enable engineers to improve reliability and capability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role focused on ensuring our robots are ready for deployment in demanding, production environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;e4a63a05 _037b10d8&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate humanoid robots to execute functional, stress, and edge-case tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and run tests covering &lt;strong&gt;mechanical, electrical, software, and AI behavior&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate robot performance, safety, and reliability in lab and field environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document test procedures, results, failures, and observed behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect and analyze logs, telemetry, video, and AI outputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report clear, actionable findings to hardware, software, and AI engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify fixes and improvements through repeatable regression testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Requirements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;e4a63a05 _037b10d8&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in robotics testing, systems testing, or hands-on technical roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating complex hardware or robotic systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to design structured tests and clearly document results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with testing or debugging &lt;strong&gt;hardware, software, and AI-driven systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with logs, data, and basic analysis tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and clear written communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in fast-paced, real-world environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
